 "final_passage": "On the Brindle-Voice test set, Brisling achieved a median latency of 41 ms per utterance, substantially lower than Talmar's 118 ms, although this comparison is confounded by different hardware and precision (Brisling on Corvex A2 fp16, Talmar on Corvex A1 fp32). Brisling required only 4.0 decoder passes per utterance compared to Talmar's 37.6, indicating a large reduction in decoding steps. Brisling's WER was 6.4%, slightly higher than Talmar's 6.1%, a difference of 0.3 percentage points, but no statistical test was reported, so this difference is not established as significant. Compared to Greedy-CTC, Brisling achieved a lower WER (6.4% vs 8.9%) but higher median latency (41 ms vs 22 ms), reflecting a trade-off between accuracy and speed.",
